me": "Jeff Greenberg", "adult": false, "gender": 2, "credit_id": "5701711c925141607f0005f3", "department": "Production", "popularity": 0.9777, "profile_path": null, "original_name": "Jeff Greenberg", "known_for_department": "Production"}, {"id": 43422, "job": "Director of Photography", "name": "James R. Bagdonas", "adult": true, "gender": 2, "credit_id": "570171449251416070000672", "department": "Camera", "popularity": 1.4, "profile_path": "/xiEqsNlhxP1JsYmxumluiqEjR99.jpg", "original_name": "James R. Bagdonas", "known_for_department": "Camera"}, {"id": 1392978, "job": "Script Supervisor", "name": "Iwona Sapienza", "adult": false, "gender": 1, "credit_id": "570174539251416072000659", "department": "Directing", "popularity": 0.1044, "profile_path": "/yL6TzbgdgyP9S8lQcqK6HIWWB2n.jpg", "original_name": "Iwona Sapienza", "known_for_department": "Directing"}, {"id": 1148734, "job": "Casting Associate", "name": "Allen Hooper", "adult": false, "gender": 0, "credit_id": "57017485c3a36856ab00067f", "department": "Production", "popularity": 0.0535, "profile_path": null, "original_name": "Allen Hooper", "known_for_department": "Production"}, {"id": 1396413, "job": "Sound Re-Recording Mixer", "name": "Dean Okrand", "adult": false, "gender": 2, "credit_id": "570174b89251416077000754", "department": "Sound", "popularity": 0.0286, "profile_path": null, "original_name": "Dean Okrand", "known_for_department": "Sound"}]}, "seasons": [{"id": 147409, "name": "Specials", "air_date": null, "overview": "", "poster_path": "/k6qEnQ8xyQnFvTcULDlrzETQRgs.jpg", "vote_average": 0, "episode_count": 63, "season_number": 0}, {"id": 3751, "name": "Season 1", "air_date": "2009-09-23", "overview": "Modern Family takes a refreshing and funny view of what it means to raise a family in this hectic day and age.  Multi-cultural relationships, adoption, and same-sex marriage are just a few of the timely issues faced by the show’s three wildly-diverse broods.  No matter the size or shape, family always comes first in this hilariously “modern” look at life, love, and laughter.", "poster_path": "/i1KhQoI391KaEA5fKArrzoTvNDk.jpg", "vote_average": 7.6, "episode_count": 24, "season_number": 1}, {"id": 3752, "name": "Season 2", "air_date": "2010-09-22", "overview": "While fledgling fathers Cameron and Mitchell struggle with learning the ropes of parenthood, long-time parents Claire and Phil try to keep the spice in their marriage amid the chaos of raising three challenging children. Meanwhile, family patriarch, Jay, has more than his hands full with his sexy, spirited wife, Gloria, and her sensitive son.", "poster_path": "/yvBc8av9K1g5QRtBDnP5xY69jb4.jpg", "vote_average": 7.6, "episode_count": 24, "season_number": 2}, {"id": 3753, "name": "Season 3", "air_date": "2011-09-21", "overview": "As the extended Pritchett-Dunphy clan faces an uproariously unpredictable array of family vacations, holiday hassles, troublesome in-laws, and surprising secrets, they still somehow manage to thrive together as one big, loving family a even as they drive each other absolutely insane!", "poster_path": "/a4EJOG8VOV02veUIYtu4lX6FVdr.jpg", "vote_average": 7.5, "episode_count": 24, "season_number": 3}, {"id": 3755, "name": "Season 4", "air_date": "2012-09-26", "overview": "With Jay and Gloria's baby on the way and Haley going off to college, the entire Pritchett-Dunphy clan faces some major surprises as they bicker and bond over house-flipping headaches, unwanted play dates, and everything from hot-tempered hormones to in utero karaoke.", "poster_path": "/pGXlhxw31fPJ6PwvzZdIRgaSHc2.jpg", "vote_average": 7.7, "episode_count": 24, "season_number": 4}, {"id": 3756, "name": "Season 5", "air_date": "2013-09-25", "overview": "Wedding bells are ringing in season five of Modern Family. As Cam and Mitchell bicker over plans for their big day, the rest of the family has its hands full adapting to new jobs, new schools, and a new male nanny.  There are babysitting disasters, an anniversary to celebrate, misguided male bonding, and everything from high-stakes poker to high-maintenance in-laws.", "poster_path": "/sJ9PqGDvGIOwJfSle62yGGieZC1.jpg", "vote_average": 7.7, "episode_count": 24, "season_number": 5}, {"id": 62023, "name": "Season 6", "air_date": "2014-09-24", "overview": "The honeymoon is over, but the laughs continue in season six of Modern Family. As freshly hitched Cam and Mitch acclimate to the realities of wedded bliss, Phil and Claire find their marriage stressed by annoying neighbors, Thanksgiving dinner gone awry and Claire's online snooping. Meanwhile, a spy-camera drone wreaks havoc in Jay and Gloria's backyard and a close call on the highway leads to amusing changes in various members of the Pritchett-Dunphy clan.", "poster_path": "/5cUUBx6iUrWFvJ8BmP2d4SATy1G.jpg", "vote_average": 7.4, "episode_count": 24, "season_number": 6}, {"id": 68804, "name": "Season 7", "air_date": "2015-09-23", "overview": "Enjoy a new chapter of love and laughter with the Seventh Season of the show. Quackery rules the roost when Phil adopts a trio of orphan ducklings and the rebellious Dunphy kids spread their wings. Meanwhile, Cam and Mitchell face financial hurdles and wild frat boys, Jay and Gloria 1farm2 out Joe2s preschool education and Manny leaps into the dating game. But will the big question finally be answered: are Haley and Andy destined to be together.", "poster_path": "/825aF6sf43gIyPsX0oeNNhqMzuH.jpg", "vote_average": 7.5, "episode_count": 22, "season_number": 7}, {"id": 78515, "name": "Season 8", "air_date": "2016-09-21", "overview": "The household hilarity continues as the Dunphy clan is wrapping up a Big Apple adventure. Back at home, Claire struggles to keep order at Pritchett's Closets while Phil and Jay go into business together. Gloria's hot sauce business heats up, as Cam and Mitchell deal with their maturing tween, Lily. Meanwhile, Manny and Luke fumble through their senior year of high school.", "poster_path": "/coOmsK9sWpScfLDlRXQ2xUJdzZ8.jpg", "vote_average": 7, "episode_count": 22, "season_number": 8}, {"id": 91749, "name": "Season 9", "air_date": "2017-09-27", "overview": "The outrageous ninth season revolves around the blended Pritchett-Dunphy-Tucker clan, headed by Jay Pritchett. Jay and his vivacious second wife Gloria are raising their young son Joe and Gloria's college bound son Manny. Meanwhile, Jay's grown daughter Claire and her husband Phil are becoming empty nesters, while Clare's brother Mitchell and his husband Cameron fumble through nurturing their gifted daughter Lily.", "poster_path": "/gLAcu4VPCAb90oJvJ4nUJc5ZBQi.jpg", "vote_average": 6.8, "episode_count": 22, "season_number": 9}, {"id": 108448, "name": "Season 10", "air_date": "2018-09-26", "overview": "As the tenth season kicks off, Jay's slated to be grand marshal in a Fourth of July parade, prompting the Pritchett-Dunphy-Tuckers to set off a few too many fireworks. Phil stumbles into a new career opportunity, while Claire grapples with her potentially changing role in the family. Meanwhile, Gloria obsesses over Manny's relationship and Joe's extracurricular activities. The extended family deals with death, but they also evolve, with more laughs than ever.", "poster_path": "/mXYC6CZ3uhGMSke1ysxp1elTmDl.jpg", "vote_average": 6.9, "episode_count": 22, "season_number": 10}, {"id": 127046, "name": "Season 11", "air_date": "2019-09-25", "overview": "Jay and Gloria are navigating life with their youngest son, Joe, while Manny has headed off to college to explore the world on his own terms. Meanwhile, Claire and Phil have officially lost their status as empty-nesters when Haley started her own family and moved back home with her new husband, Dylan, and a set of twins. Luke, is now looking to his next move; and Alex is learning how to balance life outside of academia. Then there’s Mitchell and Cameron, who are still working to understand their gifted teenage daughter, Lily, and juggle busy careers.", "poster_path": "/sMIhyJw2s1PRS8S7UtVnQrHAlNB.jpg", "vote_average": 7.3, "episode_count": 18, "season_number": 11}], "similar": {"page": 1, "results": [{"id": 46406, "name": "Family Tree", "adult": false, "overview": "Having recently lost his job and his girlfriend, 30-year-old Tom Chadwick has a rather unsure sense of his own identity. But when he inherits a mysterious box of belongings from a great aunt he never met, Tom starts investigating his lineage and uncovers a whole world of unusual stories and characters, acquiring a growing sense of who he and his real family are.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 1.7432, "vote_count": 37, "poster_path": "/aR1QlhiZVPxey4Hb5WxjJI8bpue.jpg", "vote_average": 6.4, "backdrop_path": "/u3hJeCE3OXfm8EFulQaMai6OnnH.jpg", "original_name": "Family Tree", "first_air_date": "2013-05-12", "origin_country": ["GB", "US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 46432, "name": "Sabrina: Secrets of a Teenage Witch", "adult": false, "overview": "Sabrina: Secrets of a Teenage Witch is an American animated television series on Hub Network based on the Archie Comics character Sabrina the Teenage Witch. The series is developed by Pamela Hickey and Dennys McCoy and was acquired by Hub Network on October 1, 2012. The series was originally intended for a summer 2013 release but has since been pushed out to fall 2013.", "genre_ids": [16, 35, 10759, 10765, 10762], "popularity": 1.2867, "vote_count": 8, "poster_path": "/hLr90mN4cPBGadvd5ofZtWIKAIa.jpg", "vote_average": 6.6, "backdrop_path": "/3tR5R1HrvU1St3HfSE8SqR1EIVu.jpg", "original_name": "Sabrina: Secrets of a Teenage Witch", "first_air_date": "2013-10-12", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 46444, "name": "Way to Go", "adult": false, "overview": "A black comedy about three ordinary guys who find themselves, forced by an extraordinary set of circumstances, into setting up an assisted-suicide business.", "genre_ids": [35, 18], "popularity": 0.6191, "vote_count": 9, "poster_path": "/lRZTK6dMVQ8q0zwYRMLjctPfOJt.jpg", "vote_average": 6.3, "backdrop_path": null, "original_name": "Way to Go", "first_air_date": "2013-01-17", "origin_country": ["GB"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 168, "name": "Are You Being Served?", "adult": false, "overview": "This comedy series, which follows the exploits of employees at London's fictional \\"Grace Brothers\\" department store, is full of sexual innuendo, slapstick, visual gags, and double entendres. Much of the show's humor parodies Britain's class system, and many of the show's characters are based on stereotypes of the period, including the effeminate Mr. Humphries and the rich, but stingy, store owner.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 3.8809, "vote_count": 88, "poster_path": "/kERMhisrqqSd9RfjpKDfeAi5EOj.jpg", "vote_average": 7.284, "backdrop_path": "/oO9lSt8AxrrZbvJODJtJltdXd37.jpg", "original_name": "Are You Being Served?", "first_air_date": "1972-09-08", "origin_country": ["GB"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 172, "name": "Arli$$", "adult": false, "overview": "A behind-the-scenes look at the glitzy, big-money world of professional sports following the eternally optimistic and endlessly resourceful L.A. sports agent Arliss Michaels whose Achilles' heel is his inability to say “no” to clients and employees.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 10.0629, "vote_count": 12, "poster_path": "/cJgRJdI1UsdpXEpkVtlmT0quTzm.jpg", "vote_average": 6.7, "backdrop_path": "/faukFVjVlLlwXIEhYllwdZaZOR.jpg", "original_name": "Arli$$", "first_air_date": "1996-08-10", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 175, "name": "All Along the Watchtower", "adult": false, "overview": "All Along the Watchtower is a British sitcom that aired on BBC One in 1999 about an RAF base in Scotland. It was written by Pete Sinclair and Trevelyan Evans.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 0.5491, "vote_count": 2, "poster_path": "/2fWDXT7juoCkUwW9a27whOt9b8d.jpg", "vote_average": 8, "backdrop_path": null, "original_name": "All Along the Watchtower", "first_air_date": "1999-02-28", "origin_country": ["GB"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 198, "name": "Bless This House", "adult": false, "overview": "Bless this house is a British sitcom starring Sid James and Diana Coupland that aired on ITV from the 2nd February 1971 to the 22nd April 1976. It was written by Derek Collyer, David Comming, B.C. Cummins, Harry Driver, George Evans, Dave Freeman, Carla Lane, Brian Platt, Vince Powell, Adele Rose, Mike Sharland, Bernie Sharp, Myra Taylor, Jon Watkins and Lawrie Wyman. It was made for the ITV network by Thames Television. In 2004, Bless this house came 67th in Britain's best sitcom.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 2.9949, "vote_count": 14, "poster_path": "/tJCHhmbswZ8KaBfwqELtH7thHHN.jpg", "vote_average": 7.4, "backdrop_path": "/dPD7uX8nlM0z4LsJ4mJa2ITPyhg.jpg", "original_name": "Bless This House", "first_air_date": "1971-02-02", "origin_country": ["GB"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 202, "name": "Nighty Night", "adult": false, "overview": "Nighty Night is a British dark comedy sitcom written by and starring Julia Davis. It was first broadcast on 6 January 2004 on BBC Three before moving to BBC2.\\n\\nNotorious for its dark humour, the show follows narcissistic sociopath Jill Tyrell – who manages a beauty parlour alongside her moronic, asthmatic assistant Linda – as she learns that her husband has cancer. She uses this fact to manipulate new neighbour Cathy Cole, a wheelchair user with multiple sclerosis whose husband Don, a womanising doctor, Jill has become obsessed with.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 1.8791, "vote_count": 36, "poster_path": "/nWYewaoJx8a0SbOLcX0r0KNImEf.jpg", "vote_average": 7.7, "backdrop_path": "/o1qPvtWgCzEg21oDnpHo7Mpq71a.jpg", "original_name": "Nighty Night", "first_air_date": "2004-01-06", "origin_country": ["GB"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 204, "name": "Freddie", "adult": false, "overview": "Freddie Moreno had finally escaped from the raucous house of women with whom he grew up. Having achieved some success as head chef at a trendy Chicago restaurant, he's ready for love and everything else that single life has to offer, including hanging out with his best friend and neighbor, Chris. Unfortunately, there's one slight hitch: After the death of his older brother and the collapse of his sister's marriage, goodhearted Freddie took in his impulsive sister-in-law, his pragmatic sister with her 13-year-old daughter and their irascible grandma, who refuses to speak English and only responds in Spanish – even though she understands every word. But while the members of this unconventional brood may test Freddie's patience endlessly, they also support and take care of one another, just as they always have. Now all Freddie has to do is figure out how to maintain his thriving bachelor lifestyle in a house overflowing with estrogen.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 2.689, "vote_count": 8, "poster_path": "/u9bQCwHHQ58TCK24voky5ZUMZAf.jpg", "vote_average": 4.9, "backdrop_path": "/4pkfYSKP3oQ4B7EXnmCKODgwqNM.jpg", "original_name": "Freddie", "first_air_date": "2005-10-12", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 206, "name": "Picket Fences", "adult": false, "overview": "An aging Sheriff tries to keep the peace in Rome, Wisconsin, a small town plagued by bizarre and violent crimes.", "genre_ids": [18, 35], "popularity": 6.2645, "vote_count": 51, "poster_path": "/kXJggp02MtkGdEtBfMkjI2ie3Z5.jpg", "vote_average": 7.353, "backdrop_path": "/jJHlswOAySQQijIoLqDFiIleWN6.jpg", "original_name": "Picket Fences", "first_air_date": "1992-09-18", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 220, "name": "Big Day", "adult": false, "overview": "Follows a very special day in a young couple's life, their wedding day... but tells the stories you don't see on the wedding video.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 1.7396, "vote_count": 5, "poster_path": "/35FmsYvgORNeomdRLigRJdcpF6N.jpg", "vote_average": 6, "backdrop_path": "/sJmkBP4d8Fsr41Cl00TfVHmSKb5.jpg", "original_name": "Big Day", "first_air_date": "2006-11-28", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 221, "name": "The Many Loves of Dobie Gillis", "adult": false, "overview": "The Many Loves of Dobie Gillis is an American sitcom that aired on CBS from 1959 to 1963. The series and several episode scripts were adapted from a 1951 collection of short stories of the same name, written by Max Shulman, who had also written a feature film adaptation of his short stories for MGM in 1953, The Affairs of Dobie Gillis.\\n\\nThe series revolved around the life of teenager/young adult Dobie Gillis, who, along with his best friend, beatnik Maynard G. Krebs, struggles against the forces of his life - high school, the military, college, and his parents - as he aspires to attain both wealth and dates with girls. The Many Loves of Dobie Gillis was produced by Martin Manulis Productions in association with 20th Century Fox Television. Creator Shulman also wrote the theme song in collaboration with Lionel Newman.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 7.7726, "vote_count": 15, "poster_path": "/LusZEGxE4LxIOAiBCuOvUQcLV1.jpg", "vote_average": 6, "backdrop_path": "/iIeZvExIDXBQbihb5xLeVGVHkM5.jpg", "original_name": "The Many Loves of Dobie Gillis", "first_air_date": "1959-09-29", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 227, "name": "The Mike O'Malley Show", "adult": false, "overview": "The Mike O'Malley Show is an American sitcom on NBC that aired only two episodes. The series star, Mike O'Malley, created and executive produced the series with Les Firestein.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 1.1964, "vote_count": 3, "poster_path": null, "vote_average": 8.3, "backdrop_path": null, "original_name": "The Mike O'Malley Show", "first_air_date": "1999-09-21", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 245, "name": "The Brittas Empire", "adult": false, "overview": "The Brittas Empire is a British sitcom created and originally written by Andrew Norriss and Richard Fegen. Chris Barrie plays Gordon Brittas, the well-meaning but incompetent manager of Whitbury New Town Leisure Centre.\\n\\nThe show ran for seven series and 53 episodes — including two Christmas specials — from 1991 to 1997 on BBC1. Norriss and Fegen wrote the first five series, after which they left the show.\\n\\nThe Brittas Empire enjoyed a long and successful run throughout the 1990s, and gained itself large mainstream audiences. In 2004 the show came 47th on the BBC's Britain's Best Sitcom poll, and all series have been released on DVD.\\n\\nThe creators Andrew Norriss and Richard Fegen often combine farce with either surreal or dramatic elements in episodes. For example in the first series, the leisure centre prepares for a royal visit, only for the doors to seal, the boiler room to flood and a visitor to become electrocuted. Unlike the traditional sitcom, deaths were quite common in The Brittas Empire.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 3.327, "vote_count": 41, "poster_path": "/uPtzc6MbPxeFdIO55Kd6QiiEIdH.jpg", "vote_average": 6.622, "backdrop_path": "/8o8nHTvlgdIBiOfBZ44K3JOntA9.jpg", "original_name": "The Brittas Empire", "first_air_date": "1991-01-03", "origin_country": ["GB"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 248, "name": "So Little Time", "adult": false, "overview": "So Little Time is an American sitcom starring Mary-Kate and Ashley Olsen that aired on Fox Family. The first half of the series aired from June 2, 2001, to August 15, 2001. The series then went on a four-month hiatus owing to network management changes. By December 2001, Fox Family had become ABC Family, and the remaining episodes aired until May 4, 2002.", "genre_ids": [35, 10751], "popularity": 2.491, "vote_count": 26, "poster_path": "/iNkK6WIixZlJNlMu912ngUOYTmF.jpg", "vote_average": 7.6, "backdrop_path": "/qeJUqoZZj0JUPcOhU0tseLoNFtX.jpg", "original_name": "So Little Time", "first_air_date": "2001-06-02", "origin_country": ["US"