, "original_name": "Kate Miner", "known_for_department": "Acting"}], "crew": [{"id": 80161, "job": "Executive Producer", "name": "Iain B. MacDonald", "adult": false, "gender": 2, "credit_id": "681109e25ad0b67c66eb168c", "department": "Production", "popularity": 0.2802, "profile_path": "/cxCwbSjnomHNGgvW2EP6YSr4hXv.jpg", "original_name": "Iain B. MacDonald", "known_for_department": "Directing"}, {"id": 1219549, "job": "Executive Producer", "name": "Andrew Stearn", "adult": false, "gender": 2, "credit_id": "67db30409f358f4a137f82b2", "department": "Production", "popularity": 0.1029, "profile_path": null, "original_name": "Andrew Stearn", "known_for_department": "Production"}]}, "seasons": [{"id": 45139, "name": "Specials", "air_date": "2010-12-12", "overview": "Shameless: Hall of Shame: The six-episode series will feature original Shameless scenes juxtaposed with a retrospective look at each character's journey over the prior 10 seasons. Look back at Ian, Mickey, Kev, V, Lip, Tami, Debbie, Carl, Liam, Fiona and Frank.", "poster_path": "/mEsacM6KmTf6z9kDVMisXw0EGmR.jpg", "vote_average": 0, "episode_count": 39, "season_number": 0}, {"id": 45137, "name": "Season 1", "air_date": "2011-01-09", "overview": "Frank goes missing and turns up in Toronto, tries without success to embrace sobriety, and bends the law to protect his disability checks. Fiona falls for Steve, a handsome player with a nice car, a fat wallet, and a big secret. Ian embraces his sexuality, much to the chagrin of his brainy brother Lip. Debbie goes too far at a child's birthday party. Monica shows up with an announcement about baby Liam.", "poster_path": "/gJdT0Hm5nhoAnNkgWTh6Oxusvnq.jpg", "vote_average": 7.9, "episode_count": 12, "season_number": 1}, {"id": 45138, "name": "Season 2", "air_date": "2012-01-08", "overview": "Frank and Monica rekindle their self-destructive relationship after Frank's mother returns from prison to wreak havoc. Fiona is thrown for a loop when Steve returns from Rio with a surprise. Lip makes big changes in preparation for the arrival of his and Karen's baby. Karen and Sheila clash over Karen's new husband Jody, a good-hearted but weird guy she met in Sexaholics Anonymous. Ian tries to get into West Point. Debbie prepares for the onset of puberty. Kev and Veronica contemplate starting a family.", "poster_path": "/k8QLDHT1v65ONfIrKk3jPV4AlTA.jpg", "vote_average": 7.6, "episode_count": 12, "season_number": 2}, {"id": 45140, "name": "Season 3", "air_date": "2013-01-13", "overview": "Season three finds each member of the Gallagher family seeking their individual version of the “American Dream.” Jimmy has moved into the Gallagher home, and Fiona is beginning to realize that a long-term relationship isn’t nearly as fulfilling as she expected… and her GED will only get her so far. Meanwhile, Frank reappears south of the border, with no idea how he got there.", "poster_path": "/ipeHq0WHa3B89xBY4UqzMO4aBNM.jpg", "vote_average": 7.7, "episode_count": 12, "season_number": 3}, {"id": 45141, "name": "Season 4", "air_date": "2014-01-12", "overview": "The crazy Gallaghers returned. They have new issues. Lip went to college. Fiona’s life is gradually improving. She has a stable job. The whole family is waiting for news about the health of Frank. Can the Gallaghers finally realize the middle class American dream? This ain’t no tea party.", "poster_path": "/h61CczBVTmX10MFu1ui2FDEvwUa.jpg", "vote_average": 8, "episode_count": 12, "season_number": 4}, {"id": 63466, "name": "Season 5", "air_date": "2015-01-11", "overview": "Season five finds the Gallaghers dealing with both the upside and downside of personal and urban renewal. As their neighborhood begins a move towards gentrifying, the Gallagher clan begins to reconcile their chaotic past in the hopes of building a better future.", "poster_path": "/xFm1CEG7k03SrVMj4ZG1cdd6hb3.jpg", "vote_average": 8.3, "episode_count": 12, "season_number": 5}, {"id": 70404, "name": "Season 6", "air_date": "2016-01-10", "overview": "Season six picks up a few months after last season’s finale, as the Gallaghers prepare for yet another long Chicago winter. Frank is still mourning his big loss, while his newfound appreciation for life is freaking the Gallaghers out. This season sees more than just the arctic Lake Michigan winds whipping through the Southside. Carl’s out of juvie. While Fiona struggles with a still-unstable Ian to take his meds, she’s also got another situation looming as Debbie faces a brand new baby-mama-drama.", "poster_path": "/AnYPLrl7Dxx8uXoLhsmEGPD38Fp.jpg", "vote_average": 8.1, "episode_count": 12, "season_number": 6}, {"id": 77841, "name": "Season 7", "air_date": "2016-10-02", "overview": "The Gallaghers have always scraped by, but season seven finds some of them finally getting a leg up, with more changes than the Chicago River. When Frank awakens from a coma to learn that his loved ones tossed him in the river, he declares war – Gallagher vs. Gallagher. But Fiona is too busy improving her own life to worry about Frank’s. Gallagher Golden Boy Lip finishes up his time in rehab, and emerges with a new outlook on alcoholism and his future, whereas the once-unstable Ian is now thriving as an EMT and in a comfortable relationship. Debbie is still figuring out how to be a good mom to young Franny, while Carl has some big decisions to face as he enters manhood.", "poster_path": "/8x0JX3E5LjA8Atzz359UObWaB9Z.jpg", "vote_average": 7.4, "episode_count": 12, "season_number": 7}, {"id": 91214, "name": "Season 8", "air_date": "2017-11-05", "overview": "In season 8 the Gallaghers are finally on an upswing! Frank tries to become a contributing member of society, Fiona finds success as a landlord, Lip struggles to stay sober, Ian takes up a cause, and Debbie tries life as a working single mom.", "poster_path": "/uxj2C6ilP63crohB60pjfn3pSsd.jpg", "vote_average": 7.8, "episode_count": 12, "season_number": 8}, {"id": 104861, "name": "Season 9", "air_date": "2018-09-09", "overview": "In season 9, political fervor hits the South Side, and the Gallaghers take justice into their own hands. Frank sees financial opportunity in campaigning and Fiona tries to build on the success of her apartment building.", "poster_path": "/f322ygNiP6bMGu5oo9G5wieHaV2.jpg", "vote_average": 7.9, "episode_count": 14, "season_number": 9}, {"id": 128829, "name": "Season 10", "air_date": "2019-11-10", "overview": "Season ten picks up six months after last season’s finale: Frank uses his leg injury to collect as many prescription drugs as possible and his exploits lead him to an old friend. Debbie rules over the Gallagher household with an iron fist. Lip navigates his relationship with Tami. And Gallavich returns as Ian and Mickey rekindle their relationship in prison as both cellmates and lovers.", "poster_path": "/jNMceYdwAasW8jybOtsRNzJcR2r.jpg", "vote_average": 7.3, "episode_count": 12, "season_number": 10}, {"id": 142132, "name": "Season 11", "air_date": "2020-12-06", "overview": "As Frank confronts his own mortality and family ties in his alcoholic and drug induced twilight years, Lip struggles with the prospect of becoming the family’s new patriarch. Newlyweds Ian and Mickey are figuring out the rules and responsibilities of being in a committed relationship while Deb embraces her individuality and single motherhood. Carl finds an unlikely new career in law enforcement and Kevin and V struggle to decide whether a hard life on the South Side is worth fighting for.", "poster_path": "/9akij7PqZ1g6zl42DQQTtL9CTSb.jpg", "vote_average": 6.8, "episode_count": 12, "season_number": 11}], "similar": {"page": 1, "results": [{"id": 46415, "name": "A Moody Christmas", "adult": false, "overview": "Focused on the lovable, yet seasonally dysfunctional Moody family, A Moody Christmas is set against the backdrop of the one occasion that can bring out the best (and the worst) in people … Christmas Day.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 1.1004, "vote_count": 10, "poster_path": "/lSWNWUX1LTKittrghwTer4Q7nvn.jpg", "vote_average": 8.2, "backdrop_path": "/rgrdf2aIzN7PmjGu7HPz5YkXrY8.jpg", "original_name": "A Moody Christmas", "first_air_date": "2012-10-31", "origin_country": ["AU"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 72124, "name": "Ackley Bridge", "adult": false, "overview": "A new academy school in a Yorkshire mill town merges the lives and cultures of the largely divided white and Asian community", "genre_ids": [18], "popularity": 3.2466, "vote_count": 26, "poster_path": "/fWaIn456K1rDjlfSLJJquLpmqjL.jpg", "vote_average": 7.212, "backdrop_path": "/1qDk8zVhlQS6eg4Qw4brepEtYDZ.jpg", "original_name": "Ackley Bridge", "first_air_date": "2017-06-07", "origin_country": ["GB"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 72125, "name": "Date My Dad", "adult": false, "overview": "Since the loss of his beloved Isabella three years ago, Ricky Cooper's only agenda has been to be the best dad he can be. But little does Ricky realize that his girls have an agenda of their own: get dad a girlfriend.", "genre_ids": [18], "popularity": 1.3963, "vote_count": 4, "poster_path": "/r02SV1QgRGfRsEWQZgWYSc28SW6.jpg", "vote_average": 6.5, "backdrop_path": "/aTzd5Bin2EIfZr3auY8pfp8Ak5F.jpg", "original_name": "Date My Dad", "first_air_date": "2017-06-02", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 186, "name": "Weeds", "adult": false, "overview": "After the unexpected death of her husband, a suburban mom resorts to selling weed to support her family.", "genre_ids": [35, 80, 18], "popularity": 16.8313, "vote_count": 923, "poster_path": "/gKUsBTa5b0GY7U4iWBseeBalfjO.jpg", "vote_average": 7.492, "backdrop_path": "/6k6vAUa0Fm73HB0QBOJbFGTgPq5.jpg", "original_name": "Weeds", "first_air_date": "2005-08-07", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 204, "name": "Freddie", "adult": false, "overview": "Freddie Moreno had finally escaped from the raucous house of women with whom he grew up. Having achieved some success as head chef at a trendy Chicago restaurant, he's ready for love and everything else that single life has to offer, including hanging out with his best friend and neighbor, Chris. Unfortunately, there's one slight hitch: After the death of his older brother and the collapse of his sister's marriage, goodhearted Freddie took in his impulsive sister-in-law, his pragmatic sister with her 13-year-old daughter and their irascible grandma, who refuses to speak English and only responds in Spanish – even though she understands every word. But while the members of this unconventional brood may test Freddie's patience endlessly, they also support and take care of one another, just as they always have. Now all Freddie has to do is figure out how to maintain his thriving bachelor lifestyle in a house overflowing with estrogen.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 2.689, "vote_count": 8, "poster_path": "/u9bQCwHHQ58TCK24voky5ZUMZAf.jpg", "vote_average": 4.9, "backdrop_path": "/4pkfYSKP3oQ4B7EXnmCKODgwqNM.jpg", "original_name": "Freddie", "first_air_date": "2005-10-12", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 269, "name": "One Tree Hill", "adult": false, "overview": "In Tree Hill, North Carolina two half brothers share a last name and nothing else. Brooding, blue-collar Lucas is a talented street-side basketball player, but his skills are appreciated only by his friends at the river court. Popular, affluent Nathan basks in the hero-worship of the town, as the star of his high school team. And both boys are the son of former college ball player Dan Scott whose long ago choice to abandon Lucas and his mother Karen, will haunt him long into his life with wife Deb and their son Nathan.", "genre_ids": [18], "popularity": 25.6761, "vote_count": 538, "poster_path": "/sOrelBaAhp7DZbPTivDwKEyPslC.jpg", "vote_average": 7.787, "backdrop_path": "/eDNSgT1xPMKYcEzJ5GG0PCE3NcN.jpg", "original_name": "One Tree Hill", "first_air_date": "2003-09-23", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 316, "name": "Maniac Mansion", "adult": false, "overview": "Maniac Mansion was a Canadian sitcom created by Eugene Levy, which aired concurrently on YTV in Canada and The Family Channel in the United States for three seasons from September 17, 1990 to April 4, 1993.\\n\\nThe series is very loosely based on the popular 1987 LucasArts video game of the same name. While LucasFilm served as co-producers on the series, the show thematically shares little in common with its source material.\\n\\nThe series followed the adventures of the Edison family, who lived in a large mansion in an upper-class suburban neighborhood. Fred, the father of the family, was an eccentric scientist, and many of the plots revolved around his wacky experiments. One of these experiments caused his toddler son, Turner, to transform into a large adult man and his brother-in-law, Harry, to be turned into a fly with a human head! They both remained this way for the entire run of the series.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 2.4765, "vote_count": 7, "poster_path": "/8GMqddbgAVH129mkuevOaZLPLCI.jpg", "vote_average": 4.7, "backdrop_path": "/bOkk45VacJdxTUepRsgntKbcotE.jpg", "original_name": "Maniac Mansion", "first_air_date": "1990-09-17", "origin_country": ["CA", "US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 695, "name": "Round the Twist", "adult": false, "overview": "Round the Twist is a Logie Award-winning Australian children's television series about three children and their father who live in a lighthouse and become involved in many bizarre magical adventures.", "genre_ids": [35, 10762, 10765, 99], "popularity": 3.0526, "vote_count": 25, "poster_path": "/nxOScaEU2exYLBkqG8LiYL69z5l.jpg", "vote_average": 7, "backdrop_path": "/qYitUEDAV8et1Y60XIYgel5rP3M.jpg", "original_name": "Round the Twist", "first_air_date": "1990-04-06", "origin_country": ["AU", "DE", "FR"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 72735, "name": "The Detail", "adult": false, "overview": "Three fiercely talented female homicide investigators work tirelessly to solve crimes while navigating the complicated demands of their personal lives.", "genre_ids": [80, 18], "popularity": 1.8222, "vote_count": 17, "poster_path": "/9Ec8QfalJdDDWoAGTTjMH1V3PTD.jpg", "vote_average": 6.4, "backdrop_path": "/uuZwhJYs2zTVcmLfsSRGR9qyy1Q.jpg", "original_name": "The Detail", "first_air_date": "2018-03-25", "origin_country": ["CA"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 46975, "name": "Crossing Lines", "adult": false, "overview": "Through globalization, many countries have been opened and barriers removed to ensure easy trade, travel and cultural diversity. However, this openness has given opportunities to criminals looking to exploit the system and ultimately threaten our global safety. As Europe has become a \\"safe house\\" for criminals eluding law enforcers, a special kind of law enforcement team is needed to handle specific ongoing crimes on a global level. \\"Crossing Lines\\" is the story of one such team, made up of five international cops, headed by Captain Daniel. The team - comprised of individuals who have little in common - must learn to live and work under the most dangerous and potentially deadly conditions. Housed in an unused storage section underneath the ICC, this mismatched team faces bureaucratic, jurisdictional and cultural obstacles while traversing continents in pursuit of justice.", "genre_ids": [10759, 80, 18], "popularity": 6.4917, "vote_count": 115, "poster_path": "/ow8RQrZJUQfOeR5alsj9OAXoxic.jpg", "vote_average": 6.648, "backdrop_path": "/46CHPlDDTRNyMuSMQ64FS4nUrtM.jpg", "original_name": "Crossing Lines", "first_air_date": "2013-08-22", "origin_country": ["DE", "BE", "FR", "US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 99047, "name": "Record of Youth", "adult": false, "overview": "In a cutthroat world where the life you’re born into decides your success, three aspiring youths are determined to change that perception as they fight for their dreams.", "genre_ids": [18], "popularity": 4.0883, "vote_count": 230, "poster_path": "/54yTLS5d4OPOuunzOvHlmP82eIT.jpg", "vote_average": 8.061, "backdrop_path": "/18ypvPahjmmue1iR4N4YgTBrO8N.jpg", "original_name": "청춘기록", "first_air_date": "2020-09-07", "origin_country": ["KR"], "original_language": "ko"}, {"id": 201043, "name": "Night's Stars", "adult": false, "overview": "", "genre_ids": [18], "popularity": 0.6772, "vote_count": 0, "poster_path": "/erpJUvXGpFrhpOC7peAwDmFUqWM.jpg", "vote_average": 0, "backdrop_path": null, "original_name": "نجوم الليل", "first_air_date": "2009-08-21", "origin_country": ["TN"], "original_language": "ar"}, {"id": 47091, "name": "That Winter, the Wind Blows", "adult": false, "overview": "Circumstances condemn Oh Soo and Oh Young to loveless lives. After the untimely death of his first love, Oh Soo turns to an ambitionless life as a derelict gambler. The gorgeous Oh Young should be leading the perfect life as an heiress, but when her parents’ divorce crumbles the family, she faces the reality of living life alone—particularly in light of her increasingly impaired vision. When these two heavy souls cross paths, fate delivers a chance meeting that will change their lives forever.", "genre_ids": [18], "popularity": 2.9947, "vote_count": 35, "poster_path": "/ibBjm3Bh4hw0uo4sTyK6cwzCRjg.jpg", "vote_average": 7.2, "backdrop_path": "/af37ZYhNIUy7FRWsjrmPhITfPtd.jpg", "original_name": "그 겨울, 바람이 분다", "first_air_date": "2013-02-13", "origin_country": ["KR"], "original_language": "ko"}, {"id": 23621, "name": "Police Story", "adult": false, "overview": "Police Story is an anthology series, that aired in late 1988 as part of the 'ABC Monday Mystery Movie' line-up. The crime drama is a revival of the original Police Story series (1973–1979), using previous scripts for all five two-hour episode remakes.", "genre_ids": [18, 80], "popularity": 0.4221, "vote_count": 0, "poster_path": null, "vote_average": 0, "backdrop_path": null, "original_name": "Police Story", "first_air_date": "1988-10-29", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 23656, "name": "Sherman Oaks", "adult": false, "overview": "Sherman Oaks is an adult comedy that premiered on Showtime in the summer of 1995. A second season ran in the summer of 1996. The show focused on the Sanford Baker Family of earthquake ravaged Sherman Oaks, California.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 1.5226, "vote_count": 1, "poster_path": "/tHJbAEHO0qz5prINfLy9NrwOLjm.jpg", "vote_average": 5, "backdrop_path": null, "original_name": "Sherman Oaks", "first_air_date": "1995-07-16", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 98657, "name": "61st Street", "adult": false, "overview": "Moses Johnson is a promising high-school athlete with a bright future who’s accused of murdering a police officer during a drug bust gone wrong. Swept up into the infamously corrupt Chicago criminal justice system, Moses’ case is taken up by ageing public defender Franklin Roberts, who sees this as his chance to finally challenge the institutional racism at the heart of the judicial system.", "genre_ids": [18, 80], "popularity": 1.8948, "vote_count": 22, "poster_path": "/bTEfmPiaDpsDu5oZKNSrhnF2ci5.jpg", "vote_average": 6.9, "backdrop_path": "/7ebnWh0t5WKK1owCcr0UZIROHjd.jpg", "original_name": "61st Street", "first_air_date": "2022-04-10", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 72340, "name": "Little Women", "adult": false, "overview": "Set against the backdrop of the American Civil War, the story follows sisters Jo, Meg, Beth and Amy March on their journey from childhood to adulthood. With the help of their mother, Marmee, and while their father is away at war, the girls navigate what it means to be a young woman: from sibling rivalry and first love, to loss and marriage.", "genre_ids": [18], "popularity": 2.7287, "vote_count": 101, "poster_path": "/c9jFRl34eqwU3VTbPrZFlNcZqXF.jpg", "vote_average": 7.144, "backdrop_path": "/hQAFYlWxwZntIo5LLJAMOxjN21y.jpg", "original_name": "Little Women", "first_air_date": "2017-12-26", "origin_country": ["GB"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 341, "name": "Brothers and Sisters", "adult": false, "overview": "The close-knit Walker family deals with struggles and triumphs.", "genre_ids": [18], "popularity": 12.2941, "vote_count": 186, "poster_path": "/d5eJF2tve9qBxxAYle1Q8S1HrUU.jpg", "vote_average": 7.1, "backdrop_path": "/wwim9vwDUrKbXeKcHSwvimWDqcy.jpg", "original_name": "Brothers and Sisters", "first_air_date": "2006-09-24", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 527, "name": "Joanie Loves Chachi", "adult": false, "overview": "Joanie Loves Chachi is an American television spin-off of the American sitcom Happy Days that was originally broadcast on ABC from March 23, 1982 to May 24, 1983. It stars Erin Moran and Scott Baio as the titular Joanie Cunningham and Chachi Arcola, respectively.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 1.8311, "vote_count": 18, "poster_path": "/kPJGFJJ6ID3vPo77nXJeZr33y9Y.jpg", "vote_average": 5.1, "backdrop_path": "/bffs3LApuDNAzGp6XKwOFI8e6dt.jpg", "original_name": "Joanie Loves Chachi", "first_air_date": "1982-03-23", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 610, "name": "Mr. Show with Bob and David", "adult": false, "overview": "A sketch comedy series starring and hosted by Bob Odenkirk and David Cross. The pair introduce most episodes as heightened versions of themselves before transitioning to a mixture of live sketches and pre-taped segments.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 4.2222, "vote_count": 83, "poster_path": "/rNPF7Zad87aXa7bQt4W4AYmnwL4.jpg", "vote_average": 7.675, "backdrop_path": "/pv8m2DVZewCU6BIC2oqPiZFgep2.jpg", "original_name": "Mr. Show with Bob and David", "first_air_date": "1995-11-03", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}], "total_pages": 3352, "total_results": 67036}, "tagline": "Living crappily ever after.", "homepage": "http://www.sho.com/shameless", "networks": [{"id": 67, "name": "Showtime", "logo_path"