-09-14", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 13781, "name": "Heathcliff and the Catillac Cats", "adult": false, "overview": "Heathcliff knows he is the best cat around! Never have we seen such self-confidence topped off with a heavy dose of vanity, cunning, ruthlessness, and a mischievous love of gags. He cruises and struts down the street and watch out any person, cat, or dog who gets in his way! Although he may terrorize the neighborhood, let an outsider try to push anyone around and he is a veritable tiger of defense. On the other side of town are The Catillac Cats, which typically revolve around leader Riff-Raff's get-rich-quick schemes or searches for food.", "genre_ids": [16, 35, 10762], "popularity": 7.1089, "vote_count": 50, "poster_path": "/AAS88x2ncjskKTm4Je1cNdrnf3.jpg", "vote_average": 6.3, "backdrop_path": "/qGTzrFc98LHRtuKD6d931rUvLeA.jpg", "original_name": "Heathcliff and the Catillac Cats", "first_air_date": "1984-09-17", "origin_country": ["CA", "US", "FR", "JP"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 12519, "name": "The Ruff and Reddy Show", "adult": false, "overview": "The Ruff and Reddy Show is a Hanna-Barbera animated series starring Ruff, a straight and smart cat voiced by Don Messick, and Reddy, a dumb and stupid dog voiced by Daws Butler. First broadcast in December 1957 on NBC, it was the first television show produced by Hanna-Barbera and presented by Screen Gems, the television arm of Columbia Pictures.", "genre_ids": [10751, 16, 35], "popularity": 2.9107, "vote_count": 11, "poster_path": "/2dj9Vvy689ZYNQQ85X2Iq3WpoXo.jpg", "vote_average": 5.7, "backdrop_path": "/iZm8NBU3iwrcaCF9QlAZ8z6MdmZ.jpg", "original_name": "The Ruff and Reddy Show", "first_air_date": "1957-12-14", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 12935, "name": "Slacker Cats", "adult": false, "overview": "The strange misadventures of Eddie and Buckley, two domesticated housecats dealing with life in the urban jungle.", "genre_ids": [