r Rex", "first_air_date": "1994-11-10", "origin_country": ["AT"], "original_language": "de"}, {"id": 1071, "name": "The Richie Rich/Scooby-Doo Show and Scrappy Too!", "adult": false, "overview": "The Richie Rich/Scooby-Doo Show and Scrappy Too! is a package show produced by Hanna-Barbera Productions in 1980 for ABC Saturday mornings. The program contained segments from Scooby-Doo and Scrappy-Doo and Richie Rich. The Scooby-Doo and Scrappy-Doo shorts represents the sixth show in which Scooby-Doo appears. This was the only Hanna-Barbera package series for which Scooby-Doo was given second billing and also notable for Richie Rich's debut in animation.", "genre_ids": [16, 10751, 10762, 9648, 35], "popularity": 2.6183, "vote_count": 33, "poster_path": "/8BIaNz6xZc0u2H5ncbYmveVqDDS.jpg", "vote_average": 9.2, "backdrop_path": "/5yW5JgYtEt5awdkUbPn1fLRmqLw.jpg", "original_name": "The Richie Rich/Scooby-Doo Show and Scrappy Too!", "first_air_date": "1980-11-08", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 1086, "name": "John from Cincinnati", "adult": false, "overview": "In Imperial Beach, California, the Yosts—a dysfunctional family of surfers—intersect with two new arrivals to the community: a dim-but-wealthy surfing enthusiast and man spurned by the Yosts years ago.", "genre_ids": [18, 10765], "popularity": 3.6396, "vote_count": 28, "poster_path": "/u8vyZyjpdoD3JtD5czaqj90ZfTt.jpg", "vote_average": 6.4, "backdrop_path": "/A7c63PQG3j3Ef5kMoRb2eNyIF12.jpg", "original_name": "John from Cincinnati", "first_air_date": "2007-06-10", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 1695, "name": "Monk", "adult": false, "overview": "Adrian Monk was once a rising star with the San Francisco Police Department, legendary for using unconventional means to solve the department's most baffling cases. But after the tragic (and still unsolved) murder of his wife Trudy, he developed an extreme case of obsessive-compulsive disorder. Now working as a private con