 who dreams of becoming a pop singer. At school she gets a new roommate, Irene (Sun Woong) who’s actually a boy. Irene’s persona is a pretty Female CF star and his actual name is Hyun Woo.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 0.8095, "vote_count": 13, "poster_path": "/j3TNH3r1VjNr7rGxEip2InBUVGP.jpg", "vote_average": 3.3, "backdrop_path": "/w1Dtmdy4N0Nt1fnKi5wukIow0YT.jpg", "original_name": "마보이", "first_air_date": "2012-08-16", "origin_country": ["KR"], "original_language": "ko"}, {"id": 168, "name": "Are You Being Served?", "adult": false, "overview": "This comedy series, which follows the exploits of employees at London's fictional \\"Grace Brothers\\" department store, is full of sexual innuendo, slapstick, visual gags, and double entendres. Much of the show's humor parodies Britain's class system, and many of the show's characters are based on stereotypes of the period, including the effeminate Mr. Humphries and the rich, but stingy, store owner.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 3.8809, "vote_count": 88, "poster_path": "/kERMhisrqqSd9RfjpKDfeAi5EOj.jpg", "vote_average": 7.284, "backdrop_path": "/oO9lSt8AxrrZbvJODJtJltdXd37.jpg", "original_name": "Are You Being Served?", "first_air_date": "1972-09-08", "origin_country": ["GB"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 172, "name": "Arli$$", "adult": false, "overview": "A behind-the-scenes look at the glitzy, big-money world of professional sports following the eternally optimistic and endlessly resourceful L.A. sports agent Arliss Michaels whose Achilles' heel is his inability to say “no” to clients and employees.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 10.0629, "vote_count": 12, "poster_path": "/cJgRJdI1UsdpXEpkVtlmT0quTzm.jpg", "vote_average": 6.7, "backdrop_path": "/faukFVjVlLlwXIEhYllwdZaZOR.jpg", "original_name": "Arli$$", "first_air_date": "1996-08-10", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 175, "name": "All Along the Watchtower", "adult": false, "overview": "All Along the Watchtower is a British sitcom that aired on BBC One in 1999 about an RAF base in Scotland. It was written by Pete Sinclair and Trevelyan Evans.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 0.5491, "vote_count": 2, "poster_path": "/2fWDXT7juoCkUwW9a27whOt9b8d.jpg", "vote_average": 8, "backdrop_path": null, "original_name": "All Along the Watchtower", "first_air_date": "1999-02-28", "origin_country": ["GB"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 198, "name": "Bless This House", "adult": false, "overview": "Bless this house is a British sitcom starring Sid James and Diana Coupland that aired on ITV from the 2nd February 1971 to the 22nd April 1976. It was written by Derek Collyer, David Comming, B.C. Cummins, Harry Driver, George Evans, Dave Freeman, Carla Lane, Brian Platt, Vince Powell, Adele Rose, Mike Sharland, Bernie Sharp, Myra Taylor, Jon Watkins and Lawrie Wyman. It was made for the ITV network by Thames Television. In 2004, Bless this house came 67th in Britain's best sitcom.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 2.9949, "vote_count": 14, "poster_path": "/tJCHhmbswZ8KaBfwqELtH7thHHN.jpg", "vote_average": 7.4, "backdrop_path": "/dPD7uX8nlM0z4LsJ4mJa2ITPyhg.jpg", "original_name": "Bless This House", "first_air_date": "1971-02-02", "origin_country": ["GB"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 202, "name": "Nighty Night", "adult": false, "overview": "Nighty Night is a British dark comedy sitcom written by and starring Julia Davis. It was first broadcast on 6 January 2004 on BBC Three before moving to BBC2.\\n\\nNotorious for its dark humour, the show follows narcissistic sociopath Jill Tyrell – who manages a beauty parlour alongside her moronic, asthmatic assistant Linda – as she learns that her husband has cancer. She uses this fact to manipulate new neighbour Cathy Cole, a wheelchair user with multiple sclerosis whose husband Don, a womanising doctor, Jill has become obsessed with.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 1.8791, "vote_count": 36, "poster_path": "/nWYewaoJx8a0SbOLcX0r0KNImEf.jpg", "vote_average": 7.7, "backdrop_path": "/o1qPvtWgCzEg21oDnpHo7Mpq71a.jpg", "original_name": "Nighty Night", "first_air_date": "2004-01-06", "origin_country": ["GB"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 204, "name": "Freddie", "adult": false, "overview": "Freddie Moreno had finally escaped from the raucous house of women with whom he grew up. Having achieved some success as head chef at a trendy Chicago restaurant, he's ready for love and everything else that single life has to offer, including hanging out with his best friend and neighbor, Chris. Unfortunately, there's one slight hitch: After the death of his older brother and the collapse of his sister's marriage, goodhearted Freddie took in his impulsive sister-in-law, his pragmatic sister with her 13-year-old daughter and their irascible grandma, who refuses to speak English and only responds in Spanish – even though she understands every word. But while the members of this unconventional brood may test Freddie's patience endlessly, they also support and take care of one another, just as they always have. Now all Freddie has to do is figure out how to maintain his thriving bachelor lifestyle in a house overflowing with estrogen.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 2.689, "vote_count": 8, "poster_path": "/u9bQCwHHQ58TCK24voky5ZUMZAf.jpg", "vote_average": 4.9, "backdrop_path": "/4pkfYSKP3oQ4B7EXnmCKODgwqNM.jpg", "original_name": "Freddie", "first_air_date": "2005-10-12", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 220, "name": "Big Day", "adult": false, "overview": "Follows a very special day in a young couple's life, their wedding day... but tells the stories you don't see on the wedding video.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 1.7396, "vote_count": 5, "poster_path": "/35FmsYvgORNeomdRLigRJdcpF6N.jpg", "vote_average": 6, "backdrop_path": "/sJmkBP4d8Fsr41Cl00TfVHmSKb5.jpg", "original_name": "Big Day", "first_air_date": "2006-11-28", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 221, "name": "The Many Loves of Dobie Gillis", "adult": false, "overview": "The Many Loves of Dobie Gillis is an American sitcom that aired on CBS from 1959 to 1963. The series and several episode scripts were adapted from a 1951 collection of short stories of the same name, written by Max Shulman, who had also written a feature film adaptation of his short stories for MGM in 1953, The Affairs of Dobie Gillis.\\n\\nThe series revolved around the life of teenager/young adult Dobie Gillis, who, along with his best friend, beatnik Maynard G. Krebs, struggles against the forces of his life - high school, the military, college, and his parents - as he aspires to attain both wealth and dates with girls. The Many Loves of Dobie Gillis was produced by Martin Manulis Productions in association with 20th Century Fox Television. Creator Shulman also wrote the theme song in collaboration with Lionel Newman.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 7.7726, "vote_count": 15, "poster_path": "/LusZEGxE4LxIOAiBCuOvUQcLV1.jpg", "vote_average": 6, "backdrop_path": "/iIeZvExIDXBQbihb5xLeVGVHkM5.jpg", "original_name": "The Many Loves of Dobie Gillis", "first_air_date": "1959-09-29", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 227, "name": "The Mike O'Malley Show", "adult": false, "overview": "The Mike O'Malley Show is an American sitcom on NBC that aired only two episodes. The series star, Mike O'Malley, created and executive produced the series with Les Firestein.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 1.1964, "vote_count": 3, "poster_path": null, "vote_average": 8.3, "backdrop_path": null, "original_name": "The Mike O'Malley Show", "first_air_date": "1999-09-21", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 245, "name": "The Brittas Empire", "adult": false, "overview": "The Brittas Empire is a British sitcom created and originally written by Andrew Norriss and Richard Fegen. Chris Barrie plays Gordon Brittas, the well-meaning but incompetent manager of Whitbury New Town Leisure Centre.\\n\\nThe show ran for seven series and 53 episodes — including two Christmas specials — from 1991 to 1997 on BBC1. Norriss and Fegen wrote the first five series, after which they left the show.\\n\\nThe Brittas Empire enjoyed a long and successful run throughout the 1990s, and gained itself large mainstream audiences. In 2004 the show came 47th on the BBC's Britain's Best Sitcom poll, and all series have been released on DVD.\\n\\nThe creators Andrew Norriss and Richard Fegen often combine farce with either surreal or dramatic elements in episodes. For example in the first series, the leisure centre prepares for a royal visit, only for the doors to seal, the boiler room to flood and a visitor to become electrocuted. Unlike the traditional sitcom, deaths were quite common in The Brittas Empire.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 3.327, "vote_count": 41, "poster_path": "/uPtzc6MbPxeFdIO55Kd6QiiEIdH.jpg", "vote_average": 6.622, "backdrop_path": "/8o8nHTvlgdIBiOfBZ44K3JOntA9.jpg", "original_name": "The Brittas Empire", "first_air_date": "1991-01-03", "origin_country": ["GB"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 248, "name": "So Little Time", "adult": false, "overview": "So Little Time is an American sitcom starring Mary-Kate and Ashley Olsen that aired on Fox Family. The first half of the series aired from June 2, 2001, to August 15, 2001. The series then went on a four-month hiatus owing to network management changes. By December 2001, Fox Family had become ABC Family, and the remaining episodes aired until May 4, 2002.", "genre_ids": [35, 10751], "popularity": 2.491, "vote_count": 26, "poster_path": "/iNkK6WIixZlJNlMu912ngUOYTmF.jpg", "vote_average": 7.6, "backdrop_path": "/qeJUqoZZj0JUPcOhU0tseLoNFtX.jpg", "original_name": "So Little Time", "first_air_date": "2001-06-02", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 249, "name": "Clarissa Explains It All", "adult": false, "overview": "Clarissa Darling is a teen girl dealing with typical pre-adolescent concerns such as school, boys, pimples, wearing her first training bra and an annoying little brother Ferguson.", "genre_ids": [35, 10762, 10751], "popularity": 3.212, "vote_count": 159, "poster_path": "/7cWvpbCMiYHLvn8ra5YooOAfigc.jpg", "vote_average": 7.8, "backdrop_path": "/2gSnqOroF5mC9vxsGCdURiXcZa5.jpg", "original_name": "Clarissa Explains It All", "first_air_date": "1991-03-23", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 251, "name": "Aqua Teen Hunger Force", "adult": false, "overview": "The surreal adventures of three anthropomorphic fast food items: Master Shake, Frylock and Meatwad, and their human nextdoor neighbor, Carl Brutananadilewski.", "genre_ids": [16, 35], "popularity": 16.1177, "vote_count": 224, "poster_path": "/jCWOkfMLsT2sGHadCkmR65MWtJu.jpg", "vote_average": 7.6, "backdrop_path": "/5QWdGKrPWJQ3WcafuYA2PXL6uQG.jpg", "original_name": "Aqua Teen Hunger Force", "first_air_date": "2000-12-30", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 252, "name": "Everybody Hates Chris", "adult": false, "overview": "Chris is a teenager growing up as the eldest of three children in Brooklyn, New York during the early 1980s. Uprooted to a new neighborhood and bused to a predominantly white middle school two-hours away by his strict, hard-working parents, Chris struggles to find his place while keeping his siblings in line at home and surmounting the challenges of junior high.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 16.865, "vote_count": 1059, "poster_path": "/4BYXh0cY3AyyUB05CTLVJO5FjCM.jpg", "vote_average": 8.068, "backdrop_path": "/qji729gwCW88RpIIWidlaLTul3V.jpg", "original_name": "Everybody Hates Chris", "first_air_date": "2005-09-22", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 255, "name": "Hi Hi Puffy AmiYumi", "adult": false, "overview": "Hi Hi Puffy AmiYumi follows the adventures of two very cool, but very different pop stars as they travel from gig to gig or just hang out in their tour bus. Being famous rock stars, Ami and Yumi tour the globe in their customized Puffy bus, a veritable condo on wheels with all the major amenities and an ever-changing interior. Ami is the peppy, positive, and resourceful one. Yumi is the hard-rocking, no-nonsense cynic with an absolutely infallible sense of cool. Together, these superstars take the world by storm with musical talent, trend-setting style and humor, despite occasional misjudgments from their well-meaning but tragically square manager, Kaz.", "genre_ids": [16, 35, 10762], "popularity": 7.3793, "vote_count": 139, "poster_path": "/dVlsQzfxewEdHpu7SiVUpRAVNyU.jpg", "vote_average": 7.295, "backdrop_path": "/16JZ5IRrA9YSxVSqWflY0nLhLwz.jpg", "original_name": "Hi Hi Puffy AmiYumi", "first_air_date": "2004-11-19", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 257, "name": "California Dreams", "adult": false, "overview": "A bunch of cool teenagers who are friends living in California form a rock band, The Dreams. Between gigs, they must deal with all kinds of big and small real-life issues such as school, family life, friends, romance, ambition, ego, jealousy, and big decisions.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 4.1745, "vote_count": 32, "poster_path": "/m2pFSd4HkkTOwVoBj6ticBCwOLJ.jpg", "vote_average": 6.9, "backdrop_path": null, "original_name": "California Dreams", "first_air_date": "1992-09-12", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}], "total_pages": 1521, "total_results": 30416}	2025-10-17 10:28:05.932	2025-10-17 10:28:05.932
