with Dog's feeble mind, they often backfire on Cat, much to his dismay. It may not show all the time but, he deeply loves, and cares for his brother Dog. Dog - Dog is the more lovable of the two brothers, Dog loves to play and party and play some more, he loves baseball and playing fetch with frisbees, balls, sticks, etc, He is very friendly, and happy, but does have a breaking point. He's very sensitive, and if he fails at something he feels horrible, and worthless", "genre_ids": [16, 35, 10762], "popularity": 10.877, "vote_count": 423, "poster_path": "/fkSCg9negcHAVO3gXohqEidqrsX.jpg", "vote_average": 7.038, "backdrop_path": "/yKHeZmJTFOp4lbWQE0iRKqKhP5X.jpg", "original_name": "CatDog", "first_air_date": "1998-04-04", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 676, "name": "Tom and Jerry Tales", "adult": false, "overview": "Tom and Jerry Tales is an American animated television series featuring the cat-and-mouse duo Tom and Jerry.", "genre_ids": [16, 10762, 35, 10751], "popularity": 6.0606, "vote_count": 139, "poster_path": "/gthxkV1MHAwqsVNLIU93MDm3ApL.jpg", "vote_average": 7.8, "backdrop_path": "/e7gXqszTL2hWhTOkGA1HIJFnSZ0.jpg", "original_name": "Tom and Jerry Tales", "first_air_date": "2006-09-23", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 899, "name": "The Wallflower", "adult": false, "overview": "It's a gorgeous, spacious mansion, and four handsome, fifteen-year-old friends are allowed to live in it for free! There's only one condition—that within three years the guys must transform the owner's wallflower niece into a lady befitting the palace in which they all live! How hard can it be? Enter Sunako Nakahara, the agoraphobic, horror-movie-loving, pockmark-faced, frizzy-haired, fashion-illiterate recluse who tends to break into explosive nosebleeds whenever she sees anyone attractive. This project is going to take more than our four heroes ever expected: it needs a miracle!", "genre_ids": [16, 35, 18], "popularity": 2.138, "vote_count": 31, "poster_path": "/zlcuBwbCHki0oWplNQhHhStYwFn.jpg", "vote_average": 6.839, "backdrop_path": "/aJcyY1F1oUhsQiA7fuDDzTyIDzf.jpg", "original_name": "ヤマトナデシコ七変化♥", "first_air_date": "2006-10-03", "origin_country": ["JP"], "original_language": "ja"}, {"id": 47480, "name": "The Tom and Jerry Show", "adult": false, "overview": "The iconic cat and mouse rivals are back in a fresh take on the classic series. Preserving the look, characters and sensibility of the original, this series shines a brightly colored, high-definition lens on the madcap slapstick and never-ending battle that has made Tom and Jerry two of the most beloved characters of all time.", "genre_ids": [10751, 16, 35, 10762], "popularity": 18.2745, "vote_count": 104, "poster_path": "/41EWXLXTZO4MLb2BL28mWZuydyq.jpg", "vote_average": 7.3, "backdrop_path": "/utqCOvMmjjMTlXNZz6PHOzRM5QP.jpg", "original_name": "The Tom and Jerry Show", "first_air_date": "2014-04-09", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 504, "name": "The Ren & Stimpy Show", "adult": false, "overview": "Ren and Stimpy are a mismatch made in animation heaven with nothing in common but a life-long friendship and an incredible knack for getting into trouble. Join them in their bizarre and gross world for some outlandish situations coupled with hilarious jokes.", "genre_ids": [16, 10765, 35, 10762, 10751], "popularity": 10.9675, "vote_count": 488, "poster_path": "/4plB7fMf1xob12ui7kpgnO3h4tJ.jpg", "vote_average": 7.628, "backdrop_path": "/c8m4NAE774Vsn5AZvn2bFarUtDX.jpg", "original_name": "The Ren & Stimpy Show", "first_air_date": "1991-08-11", "origin_country": ["CA", "US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 2207, "name": "Fawlty Towers", "adult": false, "overview": "Owner Basil Fawlty, his wife Sybil, a chambermaid Polly, and Spanish waiter Manuel attempt to run their hotel amidst farcical situations and an array of demanding guests.", "genre_ids": [35], "popularity": 4.3028, "vote_count": 751, "poster_path": "/kPQc2POZRND37H0OWgywvmJ49GN.jpg", "vote_average": 8.259, "backdrop_path": "/3G1uNDOGJWLNTOzjkdVphVlRmli.jpg", "original_name": "Fawlty Towers", "first_air_date": "1975-09-19", "origin_country": ["GB"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 2211, "name": "'Allo 'Allo!", "adult": false, "overview": "The misadventures of hapless cafe owner René Artois and his escapades with the Resistance in occupied France.", "genre_ids": [35, 10768], "popularity": 9.4709, "vote_count": 241, "poster_path": "/m42lb4UxkpaFil4bw0bqqjlWCY4.jpg", "vote_average": 7.79, "backdrop_path": "/pnyulr7wX1vEfyzScMRDAdxCwMc.jpg", "original_name": "'Allo 'Allo!", "first_air_date": "1984-09-07", "origin_country": ["GB"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 1886, "name": "Tutenstein", "adult": false, "overview": "Tutenstein is an animated television series, produced by Porchlight Entertainment for Discovery Kids based on the comic by Jay Stephens which was published in Oni Press' JetCat Clubhouse. This cartoon also airs on Jetix in Europe and Maxi TV in Turkey. It began broadcasting on November 1, 2003. The half-hour series features young mummy Tutankhamen who is awakened about 3,000 years after his accidental death and now must face that his kingdom is gone. The series is based on an idea by Jay Stephens. The name is a portmanteau of Tutankhamun and Frankenstein. On October 11, 2008 a TV movie entitled Tutenstein: Clash of the Pharaohs aired on Discovery Kids.\\n\\nThe production company, PorchLight Entertainment, which is based in Los Angeles, California, has won Emmys for the first and second seasons of the series. Irish TV production company Telegael, which is based in An Spidéal, Co Galway, also won an Emmy Award for the second season.\\n\\nThe Hub aired the show after the closure of Discovery Kids.", "genre_ids": [16], "popularity": 2.7757, "vote_count": 49, "poster_path": "/64mxPXRRQEMnPNJB9VdbbVLATdc.jpg", "vote_average": 6.8, "backdrop_path": "/6KNs2jsgJzAKS0xaeDwb3UJNZLI.jpg", "original_name": "Tutenstein", "first_air_date": "2003-11-01", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 1903, "name": "Action Man: A.T.O.M.", "adult": false, "overview": "A.T.O.M. is a French animated television series, which chronicles the adventures of five teenagers, set in the fictional Landmark City. The Alpha Teens, which consist of Axel Manning, Catalina Leone, Crey Kingston, Zack Hawkes, and Ollie Sharker, test prototype vehicles and weapons for Lee Industries, and use these prototypes to combat criminals, particularly the sadistic Alexander Paine.\\n\\nIn the United Kingdom, Australia and Latin America, the series is called Action Man A.T.O.M. and has its own comic book from Panini Comics.", "genre_ids": [10759, 16], "popularity": 6.4899, "vote_count": 22, "poster_path": "/moOsmnBXUuHrOUVAMlQjDkDtiiQ.jpg", "vote_average": 6.2, "backdrop_path": "/gQ1r7bIGC6HniH0F4YhGRQ23zdw.jpg", "original_name": "A.T.O.M. - Alpha Teens on Machines", "first_air_date": "2005-08-27", "origin_country": ["FR", "US"], "original_language": "en"}], "total_pages": 2265, "total_results": 45294}	2025-10-17 10:30:21.771	2025-10-17 10:30:21.771
