cFbE8eX59.jpg", "original_name": "Krypto the Superdog", "first_air_date": "2005-03-25", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 1567, "name": "CatDog", "adult": false, "overview": "The life and times of a cat and a dog with a unique twist: they're connected, literally. They share one body with a Dog's head at one end and Cat's head on the other. Adding to their dilemma is Cat's annoyance with Dog, mainly caused by Dog's stupidity and Cat's up-tight personality. Characters: Cat - Cat is the smarter one of the two brothers, and is always hatching some kind of plot to get his brother to calm down, so that Cat doesn't get beat around and hurt. Even though most of these plots involve messing with Dog's feeble mind, they often backfire on Cat, much to his dismay. It may not show all the time but, he deeply loves, and cares for his brother Dog. Dog - Dog is the more lovable of the two brothers, Dog loves to play and party and play some more, he loves baseball and playing fetch with frisbees, balls, sticks, etc, He is very friendly, and happy, but does have a breaking point. He's very sensitive, and if he fails at something he feels horrible, and worthless", "genre_ids": [16, 35, 10762], "popularity": 10.877, "vote_count": 423, "poster_path": "/fkSCg9negcHAVO3gXohqEidqrsX.jpg", "vote_average": 7.038, "backdrop_path": "/yKHeZmJTFOp4lbWQE0iRKqKhP5X.jpg", "original_name": "CatDog", "first_air_date": "1998-04-04", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 676, "name": "Tom and Jerry Tales", "adult": false, "overview": "Tom and Jerry Tales is an American animated television series featuring the cat-and-mouse duo Tom and Jerry.", "genre_ids": [16, 10762, 35, 10751], "popularity": 6.0606, "vote_count": 139, "poster_path": "/gthxkV1MHAwqsVNLIU93MDm3ApL.jpg", "vote_average": 7.8, "backdrop_path": "/e7gXqszTL2hWhTOkGA1HIJFnSZ0.jpg", "original_name": "Tom and Jerry Tales", "first_air_date": "2006-09-23", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 74, "name": "Fievel's American Tails", "adult": false, "overview": "Fievel's American Tails is an American/Canadian animated television series, produced by Steven Spielberg's Amblimation animation studio, Nelvana, and Universal Cartoon Studios. It aired for one season in 1992, and continued Fievel's adventures from the film An American Tail: Fievel Goes West.\\n\\nIn 1993 and 1994, MCA/Universal Home Video released twelve episodes on six VHS video-cassettes, two Laserdisc volumes. These have been the only home video releases of the cartoon, at least in the United States. In the United Kingdom, 12 episodes were released on six video-cassettes in 1995, but were in a different episode order to the United States and Vol.4 features the only episode that hasn't been released in the United States. Episodes have been released on DVD in France, Germany, and Italy. Universal currently has no plans to release the show on DVD in the United States, as of November 19, 2009.", "genre_ids": [37, 16, 10751], "popularity": 1.6886, "vote_count": 13, "poster_path": "/msWEkhcsqi0gfrIIpOonKumOkkT.jpg", "vote_average": 6.8, "backdrop_path": "/aMkB6DArzDUfKVpkBATeGWGaMn7.jpg", "original_name": "Fievel's American Tails", "first_air_date": "1992-09-12", "origin_country": ["CA", "US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 504, "name": "The Ren & Stimpy Show", "adult": false, "overview": "Ren and Stimpy are a mismatch made in animation heaven with nothing in common but a life-long friendship and an incredible knack for getting into trouble. Join them in their bizarre and gross world for some outlandish situations coupled with hilarious jokes.", "genre_ids": [16, 10765, 35, 10762, 10751], "popularity": 10.9675, "vote_count": 488, "poster_path": "/4plB7fMf1xob12ui7kpgnO3h4tJ.jpg", "vote_average": 7.628, "backdrop_path": "/c8m4NAE774Vsn5AZvn2bFarUtDX.jpg", "original_name": "The Ren & Stimpy Show", "first_air_date": "1991-08-11", "origin_country": ["CA", "US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 2085, "name": "Courage the Cowardly Dog", "adult": false, "overview": "The bizarre misadventures of a cowardly dog named Courage and his elderly owners in a farmhouse in Nowhere, Kansas.", "genre_ids": [16, 10751, 10765, 35, 10762], "popularity": 15.4038, "vote_count": 1575, "poster_path": "/dzD8EWDvtg7rBCINu0RCH5EUejh.jpg", "vote_average": 8.185, "backdrop_path": "/cFuk3BU0sid8dby05eyyBPtK4dD.jpg", "original_name": "Courage the Cowardly Dog", "first_air_date": "1999-11-12", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 2150, "name": "The Scooby-Doo/Dynomutt Hour", "adult": false, "overview": "The Scooby-Doo/Dynomutt Hour is a 60-minute package show produced by Hanna-Barbera Productions in 1976 for ABC Saturday mornings. It marked the first new installments of the cowardly canine since 1973, and contained the following segments: The Scooby-Doo Show and Dynomutt, Dog Wonder.", "genre_ids": [16, 35, 10751, 10762, 9648], "popularity": 4.0945, "vote_count": 169, "poster_path": "/7w13OFlmt6QPFEVxqs6eJwGXAZR.jpg", "vote_average": 7.926, "backdrop_path": "/tzk6NKctIOA1GyWuVPmrago05L4.jpg", "original_name": "The Scooby-Doo/Dynomutt Hour", "first_air_date": "1976-09-11", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 2228, "name": "Pinky and the Brain", "adult": false, "overview": "Pinky and Brain are genetically enhanced laboratory mice who reside in a cage in the Acme Labs research facility. Brain is self-centered and scheming; Pinky is good-natured but feebleminded. In each episode, Brain devises a new plan to take over the world, which ultimately ends in failure, usually due to Pinky's idiocy, the impossibility of Brain's plan, Brain's own arrogance, or just circumstances beyond their control.", "genre_ids": [16, 35, 10751, 10765, 10762], "popularity": 6.6446, "vote_count": 719, "poster_path": "/msVySCL9hRGaWFA0c3Bvx9WJFVV.jpg", "vote_average": 7.675, "backdrop_path": "/hHlhvZcB6B9dNSTvJouZ6M2BUNR.jpg", "original_name": "Pinky and the Brain", "first_air_date": "1995-09-09", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 25364, "name": "Bubsy", "adult": false, "overview": "", "genre_ids": [16, 35, 10762], "popularity": 0.6192, "vote_count": 5, "poster_path": null, "vote_average": 3.8, "backdrop_path": null, "original_name": "Bubsy", "first_air_date": "1993-11-28", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 259831, "name": "Ren & Stimpy", "adult": false, "overview": "This reboot of the 1991 slapstick buddy comedy of the same name centers on a skinny, temperamental chihuahua Ren and his trusting feline sidekick, Stimpy. Together, this twisted twosome find themselves in crazy absurd adventures.", "genre_ids": [16, 35, 10765], "popularity": 3.0287, "vote_count": 1, "poster_path": "/pl2xNFSvWjJGRSbHdyymDDNhrla.jpg", "vote_average": 9, "backdrop_path": "/oKyHM9xaJXU5AL1I1p2O4N2qNmO.jpg", "original_name": "Ren & Stimpy", "first_air_date": "2024-07-13", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 57532, "name": "PAW Patrol", "adult": false, "overview": "Marshall, Rocky, Rubble, Zuma and Skye are doing their best to protect the people of their town. Led by Ryder, a tech-savvy 10-year-old boy, each of them is equipped with special equipment and together they help anyone who finds themselves in trouble. No task is too big for them and no puppy is too small.", "genre_ids": [16, 10762], "popularity": 36.3646, "vote_count": 787, "poster_path": "/9S65uEjDqepU7d71CNmxIBHHdo.jpg", "vote_average": 7, "backdrop_path": "/7OrV2aAH5Yp7hA9zCCvUloLvZtl.jpg", "original_name": "PAW Patrol", "first_air_date": "2013-08-12", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 28352, "name": "The ChuckleHounds", "adult": false, "overview": "The ChuckleHounds was a BBC Children's TV Series staring the The Chuckle Brothers as dogs.", "genre_ids": [35, 10762], "popularity": 0.6637, "vote_count": 1, "poster_path": null, "vote_average": 4, "backdrop_path": null, "original_name": "The ChuckleHounds", "first_air_date": "1986-02-19", "origin_country": ["GB"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 5341, "name": "Dogtanian and the Three Muskehounds", "adult": false, "overview": "France, 17th century, under the reign of Louis XIII. Dogtanian is an impetuous and innocent peasant from Gascony, as well as a skilled swordsman, who travels to Paris with the purpose of making his dream come true: to join the Corps of Muskehounds of the Royal Guard.", "genre_ids": [16, 35, 10759, 10762], "popularity": 2.4814, "vote_count": 63, "poster_path": "/rHFBZgPpgHIXFz1jP5xdZlkmPqu.jpg", "vote_average": 7.3, "backdrop_path": "/juEqGPmRFYd5iBGS4ID2qOnXPv9.jpg", "original_name": "D'Artacán y los tres mosqueperros", "first_air_date": "1981-10-09", "origin_country": ["JP", "ES"], "original_language": "es"}, {"id": 7842, "name": "The Tom and Jerry Show", "adult": false, "overview": "The New Tom & Jerry Show is an animated television series produced for Saturday mornings by Hanna-Barbera Productions in association with Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer Television in 1975 for ABC based on the theatrical shorts and characters Tom and Jerry.", "genre_ids": [16, 10762, 10751, 35], "popularity": 5.2694, "vote_count": 1146, "poster_path": "/olhPG4SHIZuDngkQtKJBOMK9BiQ.jpg", "vote_average": 7.693, "backdrop_path": "/l9UK0JT5vcmm2RXaz7PcP9GnogA.jpg", "original_name": "The Tom and Jerry Show", "first_air_date": "1975-09-06", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 6771, "name": "All Dogs Go To Heaven: The Series", "adult": false, "overview": "All Dogs Go to Heaven: The Series is an animated television series which aired from 1996 to 1998 in syndication and on the Fox Family Channel from 1998 to 1999, with 41 half-hour episodes produced in total. It aired on Cartoon Network in 1999 to 2000. It was produced by MGM Animation and was distributed by Claster Television. Don Bluth’s 1989 animated feature All Dogs Go to Heaven featured a roguish German Shepherd named Charlie who died, went to heaven, conned his way back to Earth for vengeance on his killer Carface and then found redemption through a little orphaned girl named Ann-Marie. The film was popular with audiences, spawning a sequel, All Dogs Go to Heaven 2 and this animated series.\\n\\nThe theme song for the series is \\"A Little Heaven\\", written by Lorraine Feather and Mark Watters. The singers were Gene Miller of Nashville, Clydene Jackson-Edwards and Carmen Twillie. Most of the voice actors from the feature films reprised their roles in the series, including Dom DeLuise, Ernest Borgnine, Charles Nelson Reilly, Bebe Neuwirth, Sheena Easton and Adam Wylie. Steven Weber provided the voice of Charlie B. Barkin, who was voiced in the films by Burt Reynolds and Charlie Sheen.", "genre_ids": [16, 10762], "popularity": 2.0634, "vote_count": 13, "poster_path": "/qXsiNGhJbVLmfYaAibOMcYhGYJL.jpg", "vote_average": 5.9, "backdrop_path": "/9e9JL8pUps3LG4TdDw9eJv2n2PN.jpg", "original_name": "All Dogs Go To Heaven: The Series", "first_air_date": "1996-09-21", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}, {"id": 235973, "name": "Tom & Jerry Gokko", "adult": false, "overview": "Kawaii is topped with speedy and humorous movements, which is the real pleasure of \\"Tom and Jerry\\", who are constantly chasing each other and fighting with each other. A pop and cute chasing game begins with a Japanese original character design! Tom, a fussy cat who can't be hated, Jerry, a cute but clever mouse, and Taffy, a small and cute mouse, all transform into adorable characters, such as their favorite food. The hottest series with fun transformations!", "genre_ids": [10762, 16, 10751, 35], "popularity": 1.5467, "vote_count": 1, "poster_path": "/84zlQkxP9BOWjnaAfomySTNAmzH.jpg", "vote_average": 10, "backdrop_path": "/qVEUWxfuQSzdU7VHVtBUzMuBPKB.jpg", "original_name": "とむとじぇりーごっこ", "first_air_date": "2022-11-11", "origin_country": ["JP"], "original_language": "ja"}, {"id": 8553, "name": "Baggy Pants and the Nitwits", "adult": false, "overview": "Baggy Pants and the Nitwits is a 1977 animated series, produced by DePatie-Freleng Enterprises and broadcast on NBC.", "genre_ids": [16], "popularity": 0.7098, "vote_count": 1, "poster_path": "/hfjX8FnLora053fLJ2tEqN4kzsH.jpg", "vote_average": 6, "backdrop_path": "/9n1Z4IB8vTUeI3HLGi3z4gb901O.jpg", "original_name": "Baggy Pants and the Nitwits", "first_air_date": "1977-09-10", "origin_country": ["US"], "original_language": "en"}], "total_pages": 2262, "total_results": 45234}	2025-10-17 10:30:24.741	2025-10-17 10:30:24.741
